# Round XI Track M — KNOWN GAP (D36 unimplemented + MEMORY-UNSAFETY, HIGH).
#
# Class 4 of 4 filed by Track M — the WORST class per severity ranking (a
# memory-unsafety defect; the strongest priority argument for a dedicated
# Option A / D36-implementation round). CHAINED
# `m.lock().get().greet()` on `Mutex[Box[Speaker]]`. Same `.get().greet()`
# shape as class 3 (guard_get_bare_trait_fabricated_symbol.gg) but the outer
# Box wrapper turns the fabricated-symbol LINK failure into a RUNTIME
# SIGBUS — the code compiles clean AND links, and the crash only surfaces
# at direct-binary execution. SIGBUS ships PAST build, which is arguably
# worse than class 3's link error.
#
# Name-prefix `sound_` per the memory-safety fixture convention (siblings
# in tests/fixtures/known_gaps/: sound_guard_bare_param_mutate_undefined_symbol
# .gg, sound_guard_closure_capture_cc_fail.gg, sound_guard_get_string_
# double_free.gg, sound_readguard_write_faces_dropped.gg, …).
#
# MECHANISM: `Guard[Box[Speaker]].get()` returns a value the compiler
# treats as owned; Box's own auto-deref through the returned inner
# subsequently accesses a bus-fault memory address (likely a stale Box
# header interpreted as a raw pointer, or misaligned inner-object access).
# Under D36 (ratified 2026-07-27, `docs/define-gorget/decisions.md:1363-1381`)
# the entire chain should either dispatch correctly through the Guard →
# Box → trait auto-deref stack OR be REJECTED at check with a
# principled diagnostic — never compile-and-SIGBUS.
#
# DISTINCT FROM Track J (`sound_guard_get_string_double_free.gg` — double-free
# on non-trait heap-inner via `.get()`'s ownership contract; different
# root — that's an owned-return contract, this is a trait-dispatch +
# Box-auto-deref stack producing invalid memory access).
#
# HEAD behavior (probe 2026-07-28):
#   gg check <this>            → OK: no semantic errors (exit 0)
#   gg build <this> -o /tmp/p  → OK (exit 0; compiles and links clean)
#   /tmp/p                     → SIGBUS, direct-binary exit=135
#   gg run <this>              → exit 1 (masks the signal detail;
#                                per Core #15(d) `gg run` masks SIGSEGV/SIGBUS
#                                as a silent exit 1 — always probe the
#                                built binary directly)
#
# FIX DIRECTION (Option A / D36-implementation, DEFERRED to Round XII+):
# same as classes 1/3 — extend Guard vtable dispatch to mirror Box in
# `src/ir/lowering/exprs/methods.rs:1627-1682` AND extend Guard's `.get()`
# return-type propagation to preserve trait inners. This class merits high
# priority within Round XII's queue because it is memory-unsafety (per
# Round XI theme).
#
# INTENDED (after Option A): prints `beep R2`.

from std.collections import Box

trait Speaker:
    String greet(self)

struct Robot:
    String name

equip Robot with Speaker:
    String greet(self):
        return "beep " + self.name

void main():
    print(Mutex[Box[Speaker]](Box.new(Robot("R2"))).lock().get().greet())
